      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:4412/?q=continuity&saved=1#collection/time",
      "scrollY": 0,
      "text": "Skip to content\nIndex.\nCollections\nYour personal index\nBack to collections\nCOLLECTION 05 / 06\n\nIN THIS COLLECTION\n\nTopic\nInteraction\nCollected\n14 references\nLast updated\nOctober 24, 2026\nSaved\n\nA small place to keep\na bigger train of thought.\n\nINTERACTION\n\nKeeping your place when everything around you is changing\n\nA collection of notes about continuity, repeated action and the moments between states.\n\nCOLLECTION NOTES\n01 — 03\n\nThis collection brings together observations, references and unresolved questions from our ongoing research. It is intended for close reading and return visits rather than a linear presentation.\n\nLook for the relationships between attention, scale and context. A useful detail becomes more valuable when it survives changes in content, screen size and the way a person moves through the work.\n\nThe working notes remain provisional. Revisit the evidence, compare different contexts and keep the next useful question close to the material.\n\n✳\n\nGood questions are worth returning to.\n\nBack to your collections\nStay curious. Keep collecting.\nSample research collections · Saves stay in this browser",
